<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  A-36  Проверка обновлений.  H3 · R1.
  ============================================================================

  24-tab-conformance.md A-36 marks this screen DELETE - it was unreachable, so it
  cost nothing to cut. It is reachable now (a row in «Настройки» and one on «О
  приложении»), and it is the product's only update path: departament ships as a
  direct APK, so what happens here is what a user gets instead of a store.

  It reported its outcome in toasts once - three of them, one an exception message
  shown raw to a customer. It has states now, and every one of them is drawn:

      checking     · an inline arc and «Проверяем обновления…»
      up to date   · «Обновлений нет»
      available    · «Доступна версия X» + release notes + «Обновить»
      downloading  · a determinate bar with «12,4 МБ из 31,0 МБ» and «Отменить»
      ready        · «Обновление готово» + «Установить»
      permission   · «Нужно разрешение на установку» + «Открыть настройки»
      failed       · the MAPPED cause, and its retry immediately under it (G2)

  WHY THE ACTION IS NOT THE EMPTY STATE'S ACTION. `EmptyStateBinder` puts its button
  behind a ViewStub, and a stub inflates once - so the FIRST state that shows a
  button fixes the tier for the rest of the screen's life. On a screen that alternates
  between a Primary «Обновить» and a Tertiary «Повторить» that is a coin toss: whoever
  loses gets the wrong tier. The two tiers are therefore two <include>s here, and
  exactly ONE of them is ever visible - the component's "one action, or none" rule,
  enforced by the screen instead of by the stub.

  2026-08 REDESIGN — handoff README §7, checked against the prototype frame
  (docs/design2026/port-shots-2/48-update.png). The prototype draws this screen as:

      кнопка назад · «Проверить обновление» 24sp/700
      карточка · «Искать предварительный выпуск» (переключатель)
               · «Проверить обновление» (акцентная строка действия)
      подпись  · «departament 2.2.1»

  and this file is now that. What moved: the version stopped being a Row.Value at the
  top of the card and became the caption under it, where the prototype puts it (it
  still copies on tap, so nothing was lost but a row); «Проверить обновление» stopped
  being only an implicit consequence of opening the screen and became the accent row
  the prototype names.

  THE STATE ACTIONS STAY BUTTONS. §7's lekalo has one row per action, but «Обновить»
  / «Установить» / «Отменить» / «Повторить» change TIER between states and a row has
  one appearance. The accent row above is the CHECK; those four are the outcome, they
  live under the verdict they belong to, and turning them into rows would delete four
  of the seven states listed above.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="?android:attr/colorBackground"
    android:fitsSystemWindows="true"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    tools:context=".ui.CheckUpdateActivity">

    <include
        android:id="@+id/toolbar"
        layout="@layout/view_sub_header" />

    <androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView
        android:id="@+id/main_content"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="0dp"
        android:layout_weight="1"
        android:clipToPadding="false"
        android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_32"
        android:scrollbars="none">

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                style="@style/Widget.Departament.CardSection"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/screen_gutter">

                <LinearLayout style="@style/Widget.Departament.CardSection.Body">

                    <include
                        android:id="@+id/row_pre_release"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        layout="@layout/view_row" />

                    <com.google.android.material.divider.MaterialDivider
                        style="@style/Widget.Departament.Divider.Full"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content" />

                    <include
                        android:id="@+id/row_check"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        layout="@layout/view_row" />
                </LinearLayout>
            </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

            <!-- The installed version, as the caption the prototype draws under the card
                 («departament 2.2.1») rather than as a row of its own. It still copies on tap,
                 which is what the row it replaced did. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_version"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
                android:background="@drawable/bg_row"
                android:minHeight="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_8"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_8"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption"
                tools:text="departament 2.2.1 (25.3.6)" />

            <!-- The result block: one state at a time, never two. Both layout_width and
                 layout_height are declared because an <include> ignores every layout_*
                 attribute unless those two are present - which is how the margin above
                 would have silently done nothing. -->
            <include
                android:id="@+id/empty_state"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_32"
                layout="@layout/view_empty_state" />

            <!-- CHECKING. An indeterminate arc: there is no total to divide by. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/checking"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_32"
                android:gravity="center_horizontal"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:visibility="gone">

                <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
                    android:id="@+id/progress"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.Progress.Circular.Inline"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:indeterminate="true" />

                <TextView
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
                    android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                    android:text="@string/upd_checking"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- DOWNLOADING. The bar starts indeterminate (the size is unknown until
                 the first chunk) and becomes determinate the moment a Content-Length
                 arrives; if none ever does it keeps moving and the caption reports the
                 megabytes so far, rather than inventing a percentage. Only that
                 direction is legal at runtime - see CheckUpdateActivity.showDownloading. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/downloading"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_32"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:visibility="gone">

                <TextView
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                    android:text="@string/upd_downloading"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Body" />

                <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.LinearProgressIndicator
                    android:id="@+id/download_progress"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.Progress.Linear"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
                    android:max="100" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/download_detail"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                    tools:text="12,4 МБ из 31,0 МБ" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- What is in the new version, between the verdict and the button: the
                 user decides whether to update after reading it, not before. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_release_notes"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_16"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Body"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:text="Исправлено переподключение после смены сети."
                tools:visibility="visible" />

            <!-- The one action, in two tiers. 24 above it is the empty state's own
                 title-line-action rhythm, continued. -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/action_area"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_24"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible">

                <include
                    android:id="@+id/action_primary"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal"
                    layout="@layout/view_action_primary" />

                <include
                    android:id="@+id/action_tertiary"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal"
                    android:visibility="gone"
                    layout="@layout/view_action_tertiary" />
            </FrameLayout>
        </LinearLayout>
    </androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>
</LinearLayout>
